From 1bf84ca29c9a29a0cbc71e767982089e8180316a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 04:03:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Correct MinGW native function guard and enforce strict
 preprocessing

Use a valid identifier in the F_X86_NATIVE guard and preserve its architecture-dependent expansion. Make generated import definitions reject warnings. Include x86-64 and ARM64 regression tests through the actual hermetic Clang and MinGW inputs.

TDD: both Bazel regression targets fail on the original header with extra tokens at end of #ifndef (bazel-red.log, exit 1). Both pass after the fix (bazel-green-second.log, exit 0). Actual msvcr90d.def and ucrtbase.def generation with fatal diagnostics passes (def-generation.log, exit 0). just fmt-check passes (format.log); emitted checks are recorded separately.

Base: rust-v0.162.1, 092d3acd6bec3e3a14bdc7e7a2810ab628ab759d. Refs holdmyspot-com/codex-unleashed#61.
